    "created_at": "2017-02-05T19:21:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-02-05T19:21:44Z",
    "body": "@annevk after thinking about this for a few days, the only thing I found that this might affect the pathname return value of `Location` are internal browser pages such as those that use the `chrome://` protocol since this is not classified as a `special scheme`.  Checking the `Location` object when navigating to `chrome://version` in Chrome and Opera results in pathname being non-empty, though I would expect it to be empty after the changes made to path parsing for non-special URLs.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
